-- title:
--   Contragredient-type representative with unchanged right convolution
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field and write $G = \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ for `AdelicGL2 (𝓞 F) F`, the general linear group of rank $2$ over the adele ring of $F$. Let `tys : ArchTypeFamily F` be an archimedean type family, that is, a number `tys.card w` for each infinite place $w$ of $F$ together with, for each $i \in$ `Fin (tys.card w)`, a datum `tys.rep w i` consisting of a dimension $n$ and a representation $\rho$ of `rowIsometrySubgroup₀ w.Completion` on $\mathbb{C}^n$. Let $y : G \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous and lie in `archCutSubmodule F tys`, the intersection over all infinite places $w$ of the supremum over $i$ of the submodules `typeSubmodule (rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w) (tys.rep w i).ρ`. Let $f : G \to \mathbb{C}$ be continuous with compact support, and let $S$ denote the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the set of functions of the form `rightTranslate F k f` $= (x \mapsto f(xk))$ for $k$ in the subgroup $\bigsqcup_w$ generated by the ranges of the inclusions `rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w`; assume $S$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{C}$. Then there is an $f' \in S$ such that $f'$ lies in `archDualCutSubmodule F tys`, the intersection over $w$ of the supremum over $i$ of the submodules `typeSubmodule (rowIsometryInclAt₀ F w) (tys.rep w i).ρ.dual` attached to the contragredient representations, and such that `rightConv F y f'` $=$ `rightConv F y f`, where `rightConv F y h` is the function $g \mapsto \int_G y(gx)h(x)\,d\mu(x)$ for $\mu$ the Haar measure `AdelicHaar.adelicGLHaar (Fin 2) (𝓞 F) F` on $G$.
--
--   This is the Schur-orthogonality step for the right-convolution pairing: since $\int_G y(gx)h(x)\,dx$ is invariant under simultaneous right translation of $y$ and $h$ by the archimedean row-isometry subgroups (right invariance of the adelic Haar measure on $G$), the components of $f$ whose archimedean type is not contragredient to a type occurring in $y$ contribute nothing, so $f$ may be replaced inside the span of its translates by a function of contragredient cut type without altering the convolution. It is used in the construction of the archimedean cut projector, in [`AutomorphicForm.exists_rightConv_eq_of_archCutProjector`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_rightConv_eq_of_archCutProjector).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_exists_mem_span_rightTranslate_mem_archDualCutSubmodule_and_rightConv_eq.lean

